   "body": "Status (ext/bybifok-opus-1, Opus 5.5): **done on branch `moust4ki:lot/306-topic-delflag-link` at 94d2c0f, PR not opened yet.** The external contributor brief allows two open PRs at a time, and #318 and #319 are open. The PR will follow as soon as one of them is merged.\n\nWhat the branch does:\n- `TopicPageMetadata.flag: TopicPageFlag?` (HFRParsing). It holds the first link of the function bar `tr.fondForum2Fonctions` whose URL is exactly `https://forum.hardware.fr/user/delflag.php` (port 443, no user info), and the flag its icon names: `flagn0.gif` red, `flagn1.gif` blue, `favorisn.gif` favourite. It is `nil` without such a link (anonymous pages, private conversations).\n- The lookup is scoped to the bar. Legacy took the first `href` containing `delflag` anywhere in the body (`MessagesTableViewController.m:1559-1566`), so a link posted in a message could become the remove-flag action.\n- Tests in `TopicPageFlagTests`:\n  - the eight captures with the link (`P03m`, `R63a`, `R63e`, `R21`, `R32b`, `R33b`, `R61d`, `R61e`) and six without it;\n  - `P03m`'s link is exactly `P03n`'s request;\n  - scope, origin and icon rules, on in-memory edits of `R20` and `R21`.\n  \n  Each test was shown to fail on a mutation: flag never read, whole-body lookup as in legacy, no origin check. `swift test` passes on macOS (967 tests).\n- Docs: the LOT-033 spec (new `flag` row, difference 5 rewritten, pending-capture item removed), the HFR-PROTOCOL LOT-033 subsection and a CHANGELOG-LEGACY row.\n\nNo pending capture: the captures cover the three icons, and the two theme folders `images_forum/1/` and `images/defaut/`.\n",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
